## Phase 5 — Migrate to LangGraph `ToolNode`

### Step 5.1 — Add `toLangChainTools()` to `StructuredToolRegistry`

**File:** `backend/src/modules/tools/structured-tool.registry.ts`

```typescript
import { DynamicStructuredTool } from '@langchain/core/tools';

toLangChainTools(
  securityContext?: { tenantId: string; agentId: string; userId: string },
  securityInterceptor?: SecurityInterceptorService,
): DynamicStructuredTool[] {
  return Array.from(this.tools.values()).map(
    (tool) =>
      new DynamicStructuredTool({
        name: tool.name, description: tool.description, schema: tool.inputSchema,
        func: async (input) => {
          if (securityInterceptor && securityContext) {
            const check = await securityInterceptor.validate(tool, input, securityContext);
            if (!check.allowed) throw new Error(`Security blocked: ${check.reason}`);
            input = check.sanitizedInput ?? input;
          }
          const result = await tool.execute(input, { tenantId: securityContext?.tenantId ?? '' });
          if (!result.success) throw new Error(result.error ?? 'Tool failed');
          return JSON.stringify(result.data ?? null);
        },
      }),
  );
}
```

**SOLID:** OCP — new method; existing `register/get/execute` unchanged.

### Step 5.2 — Replace manual `toolNode` with `ToolNode` in `OfficialAgentGraph`

```typescript
import { ToolNode } from "@langchain/langgraph/prebuilt";

// In buildGraph():
const langChainTools = this.toolRegistry.toLangChainTools(
  undefined,
  this.securityInterceptor,
);
workflow.addNode(TOOL_NODE, new ToolNode(langChainTools));
```

For per-call security context: store `currentTenantId`/`currentAgentId` as mutable instance props on `OfficialAgentGraph`, updated at the start of each `run()` call, read inside `toLangChainTools()` closure. Remove the hand-written `toolNode` method.

